+# macOS presentation and input
+
+Cocoa windows now attach an SDL Metal view's CAMetalLayer to a WebGPU Metal surface. The existing surface presenter handles drawing and resize, avoiding the display-image GPU-to-CPU copy and SDL texture upload. `PS2_SDL_RENDERER=1` keeps the SDL path for comparisons and fallback. The view is released on failed attachment and at threaded-window shutdown.
+
+The log should identify the Metal adapter, the offered presentation modes and `[window] presenting through WebGPU`. A local M1 Pro run offers Fifo and Immediate and selects Immediate. A 700-frame SC3 saved-state run completed through the direct path; graphics readbacks requested by the game still occur and can stall independently of presentation. This patch does not claim to remove those readbacks.
+
+The host uses key events for gameplay and bindings, with no Unicode text-entry field. It stops SDL's default text input to avoid unused IME initialization. Replay confirms gameplay input behavior through the runtime; first-physical-key latency still needs an interactive check.
+
+API references: [SDL_Metal_CreateView](https://wiki.libsdl.org/SDL2/SDL_Metal_CreateView), [SDL_Metal_GetLayer](https://wiki.libsdl.org/SDL2/SDL_Metal_GetLayer), [SDL_StartTextInput](https://wiki.libsdl.org/SDL2/SDL_StartTextInput).
